      "path": "/books/al-kafi:3:1:33:11",
      "text": [
        " لَا بَأْسَ بِأَنْ يَحْتَجِمَ الرَّجُلُ وَ هُوَ جُنُبٌ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Ali Bin Ibrahim, from his father, from Ibn Abu Umeyr, from hammad, from Al Halby, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> having said: ‘There is no problem with, if a man were to get cupping done and he was with sexual impurity’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "11. Ali ibn Ibrahim has narrated from his father from ibn abu ‘Umayr from Hammad from al-Halabiy who has said the following: “Abu ‘Abd Allah, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, has said, ‘It is permissible for one who has experienced sexual relation to draw blood from his body by means of cupping.’” "
        ]
      }
